  The Cauchy problem for this equation models in particular the small amplitude
  movements of a string submitted for instance to an initial deformation:
  such
  deformations propagate with velocity 1 without any modiﬁcation of their shape or
  amplitude.
  In what follows, our objective is to characterize, for computational
  purpose, the restriction of the solution to the half-line x < 0 by introducing an artiﬁcial
  boundary at x = 0, assuming that the initial data are supported in this half-line. In this
  case, there is a very simple transparent condition, which is local (but this is no longer
  true in dimension > 1):
  
